  "term": "alpha-melanocyte stimulating hormone",
  "definition": "Alpha-melanocyte stimulating hormone is a neuropeptide that helps regulate immune cell activity, especially in the eye’s immunosuppressive environment. In the supplied source, it suppresses inflammatory activity in macrophages and supports their survival by reducing part of the apoptosis pathway after caspase 3 activation but before DNA fragmentation.",
